	"_note": "The hall dressing layer (world/hall_props.rs): real, solid props along the walls of wide halls on level 0, placed once when a chunk is built, after the Godot-ported generator (docs/PROP_FACING.md). A prop stands on a hall cell (open floor outside every room) with a wall behind it, its back to the wall. min_width: the hall must be this many cells wide at the prop. min_lane / min_lane_narrow: metres of hall left clear in front of the prop (narrow applies to halls of narrow_width cells or fewer; there the two cells in front must be clear, so props hug one wall). long_run: a straight wall run of this many cells counts as long and multiplies the chance by long_bonus. chance: per wall-side cell, by region (default for a region not listed). spacing: cells (Chebyshev) between two hall props. max_per_chunk caps a chunk. door_gap, stair_gap, hide_gap, pickup_gap, prop_gap, start_gap: cells kept clear round a doorway cell, a stair or ladder cell, a locker, vent or hiding prop, a pickup, any other prop and the chunk's start. edge_margin: cells kept clear along the chunk border (its openings to the next chunk). max_depth / max_width: metres; a type whose collider is larger is skipped. props: per region the types to draw from (default for a region not listed); size is [width, depth] in metres at rotation 0 and is used only when the type has no collider row in world/route/prop_tables.rs. Use types that exist in data/props and are not hiding props.",
